# Paths inside the kitty config directory that dof never touches.
#
# Only whole-line comments are recognised, same as .gitignore —
# a "#" after a pattern is part of the pattern, not a comment.

# ── Background images ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~7 MB of wallpapers against ~170 KB of actual config: adopting them would
# grow the repo roughly 40x for content that is neither portable nor shared.
#
# The consequence is deliberate and documented. Since 2026-08-30 the background
# is off by default — theme-overrides.conf no longer sets background_image, so
# nothing points at a missing file. Ctrl+middle simply finds no PNG and the
# toggle script exits 0. Dropping an image into backgrounds/ is enough to
# restore it; no config edit is needed, the script globs the directory.
# That, and why the images must be PNG (kitty bundles libpng only, every other
# format needs ImageMagick), are in ~/.config/kitty/README.md.
backgrounds/

# ── Icons ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# icons/ is the same trade as backgrounds/: image assets, not configuration.
#
# kitty.app.png is excluded for a second reason. switch-icon.py copies the
# chosen icon onto it, so under link mode that write would land straight in
# the repo — a 128 KB binary churning on every icon switch.
# Rebuilding both is switch-icon.py's whole job; README.md has the steps.
icons/
kitty.app.png

# ── Themes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All four are upstream Catppuccin (MIT) reproduced verbatim, and the only
# local content is the two lines appended at the end of each:
#
#     # 背景圖與標籤欄顏色（見 theme-overrides.conf 開頭的說明）
#     include theme-overrides.conf
#
# current-theme.conf is byte-identical to dark-theme.auto.conf, so adopting
# the set would commit the same third-party palette twice over for one line
# that is actually ours. The theme names are recorded in README.md instead —
# regenerating from them is one command per file.
#
# It also removes a recurring annoyance: the themes kitten rewrites these as
# real files, which would replace dof's symlinks and leave dof status
# reporting UNLINKED after every theme change.
current-theme.conf
*-theme.auto.conf

# ── Stale backup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A hand-made backup from before this config was tracked. The built-in
# *.dof-bak-* pattern does not cover it.
kitty.conf.bak
